(Form W-9 \(Rev. 3-2024\)   Page 2) Tj T*
(General Instructions) Tj T*
(Section references are to the Internal Revenue Code unless otherwise noted.) Tj T*
(Future developments. For the latest information about developments related to Form W-9 and its) Tj T*
(instructions, such as legislation enacted after they were published, go to www.irs.gov/FormW9.) Tj T*
(What's New) Tj T*
(Line 3a has been modified to clarify how a disregarded entity completes this line. An LLC that is a) Tj T*
(disregarded entity should check the appropriate box for the tax classification of its owner. Otherwise, it) Tj T*
(should check the "LLC" box and enter its appropriate tax classification.) Tj T*
(New line 3b has been added to this form. A flow-through entity is required to complete this line to) Tj T*
(indicate that it has direct or indirect foreign partners, owners, or beneficiaries when it provides the Form) Tj T*
(W-9 to another flow-through entity in which it has an ownership interest.) Tj T*
(Purpose of Form) Tj T*
(An individual or entity \(Form W-9 requester\) who is required to file an information return with the IRS is) Tj T*
(giving you this form because they must obtain your correct taxpayer identification number \(TIN\), which) Tj T*
(may be your social security number \(SSN\), individual taxpayer identification number \(ITIN\), adoption) Tj T*
(taxpayer identification number \(ATIN\), or employer identification number \(EIN\), to report on an) Tj T*
(information return the amount paid to you, or other amount reportable on an information return.) Tj T*
(Examples of information returns include, but are not limited to, the following.) Tj T*
(- Form 1099-INT \(interest earned or paid\).) Tj T*
(- Form 1099-DIV \(dividends, including those from stocks or mutual funds\).) Tj T*
(- Form 1099-MISC \(various types of income, prizes, awards, or gross proceeds\).) Tj T*
(- Form 1099-NEC \(nonemployee compensation\).) Tj T*
(- Form 1099-B \(stock or mutual fund sales and certain other transactions by brokers\).) Tj T*
(- Form 1099-K \(merchant card and third-party network transactions\).) Tj T*
(- Form 1098 \(home mortgage interest\), 1098-E \(student loan interest\), and 1098-T \(tuition\).) Tj T*
(Use Form W-9 only if you are a U.S. person \(including a resident alien\), to provide your correct TIN.) Tj T*
(If you do not return Form W-9 to the requester with a TIN, you might be subject to backup withholding.) Tj T*
(Payments you receive will be subject to backup withholding if you do not furnish your TIN to the) Tj T*
(requester, or the Internal Revenue Service \(IRS\) tells the requester that you furnished an incorrect TIN.) Tj T*
(Penalties) Tj T*
(Failure to furnish TIN. If you fail to furnish your correct TIN to a requester, you are subject to a penalty) Tj T*
(of $50 for each such failure unless your failure is due to reasonable cause and not to willful neglect.) Tj T*
(Line 1) Tj T*
(You must enter one of the following on this line; do not leave this line blank. The name should match the) Tj T*
(name on your tax return.) Tj T*
(Individual. Generally, enter the name shown on your tax return. If you have changed your last name) Tj T*
(without informing the Social Security Administration \(SSA\) of the name change, enter your first name, the) Tj T*
(last name as shown on your social security card, and your new last name.) Tj T*
(Sole proprietor. Enter your individual name as shown on your Form 1040 on line 1. Enter your business,) Tj T*
(trade, or "doing business as" \(DBA\) name on line 2.) Tj T*
(Limited liability company \(LLC\). If you are a single-member LLC \(including a foreign LLC with a domestic) Tj T*
(owner\) that is disregarded as an entity separate from its owner under Treasury regulations section) Tj T*
(301.7701-3, enter the owner's name on line 1. The name of the owner entered on line 1 should never be a) Tj T*
(disregarded entity. The name on line 1 should be the name shown on the income tax return on which the) Tj T*
(income should be reported.) Tj T*
(Line 3a) Tj T*
(Check the appropriate box on line 3a for the U.S. federal tax classification of the person whose name is) Tj T*
(entered on line 1. Check only one box on line 3a.) Tj T*
(IF the entity/individual on line 1 is a\(n\) . . .        THEN check the box for . . .) Tj T*
(- Corporation                                           Corporation.) Tj T*
(- Individual or Sole proprietorship                     Individual/sole proprietor.) Tj T*
(- LLC classified as a partnership for U.S. federal tax purposes or) Tj T*
(- LLC that has filed Form 8832 or 2553 electing to be taxed as a corporation) Tj T*
(                                                        Limited liability company and enter the) Tj T*
(                                                        appropriate tax classification.) Tj T*
(- Partnership                                           Partnership.) Tj T*
(- Trust/estate                                          Trust/estate.) Tj T*
(Form W-9 \(Rev. 3-2024\)) Tj T*
ET

