(Form W-9 \(Rev. 3-2024\)   Page 5) Tj T*
(Part I. Taxpayer Identification Number \(TIN\)) Tj T*
(Enter your TIN in the appropriate box. If you are a resident alien and you do not have, and are not) Tj T*
(eligible to get, an SSN, your TIN is your IRS ITIN. Enter it in the entry space for the Social security number.) Tj T*
(If you do not have an ITIN, see How to get a TIN below.) Tj T*
(If you are a sole proprietor and you have an EIN, you may enter either your SSN or EIN.) Tj T*
(If you are a single-member LLC that is disregarded as an entity separate from its owner, enter the owner's) Tj T*
(SSN \(or EIN, if the owner has one\). If the LLC is classified as a corporation or partnership, enter the) Tj T*
(entity's EIN.) Tj T*
(How to get a TIN. If you do not have a TIN, apply for one immediately. To apply for an SSN, get Form SS-5,) Tj T*
(Application for a Social Security Card, from your local SSA office or get this form online at www.SSA.gov.) Tj T*
(You may also get this form by calling 1-800-772-1213. Use Form W-7, Application for IRS Individual) Tj T*
(Taxpayer Identification Number, to apply for an ITIN, or Form SS-4, Application for Employer) Tj T*
(Identification Number, to apply for an EIN. You can apply for an EIN online by accessing the IRS website) Tj T*
(at www.irs.gov/EIN. Go to www.irs.gov/Forms to view, download, or print Form W-7 and/or Form SS-4.) Tj T*
(Or, you can go to www.irs.gov/OrderForms to place an order and have Form W-7 and/or SS-4 mailed to) Tj T*
(you within 15 business days.) Tj T*
(Secure Your Tax Records From Identity Theft) Tj T*
(Identity theft occurs when someone uses your personal information, such as your name, SSN, or other) Tj T*
(identifying information, without your permission to commit fraud or other crimes. An identity thief may) Tj T*
(use your SSN to get a job or may file a tax return using your SSN to receive a refund.) Tj T*
(If you are a victim of identity theft who is experiencing economic harm or a systemic problem, or is) Tj T*
(seeking help in resolving tax problems that have not been resolved through normal channels, you may be) Tj T*
(eligible for Taxpayer Advocate Service \(TAS\) assistance. You can reach TAS by calling the TAS toll-free) Tj T*
(case intake line at 1-877-777-4778 or TTY/TDD 1-800-829-4059.) Tj T*
(Protect yourself from suspicious emails or phishing schemes. Phishing is the creation and use of email) Tj T*
(and websites designed to mimic legitimate business emails and websites. The IRS does not initiate) Tj T*
(contacts with taxpayers via emails. Also, the IRS does not request personal detailed information through) Tj T*
(email or ask taxpayers for the PIN numbers, passwords, or similar secret access information for their) Tj T*
(credit card, bank, or other financial accounts.) Tj T*
(If you receive an unsolicited email claiming to be from the IRS, forward this message to phishing@irs.gov.) Tj T*
(You may also report misuse of the IRS name, logo, or other IRS property to the Treasury Inspector General) Tj T*
(for Tax Administration \(TIGTA\) at 1-800-366-4484. You can forward suspicious emails to the Federal Trade) Tj T*
(Commission at spam@uce.gov or report them at www.ftc.gov/complaint. You can contact the FTC at) Tj T*
(www.ftc.gov/idtheft or 877-IDTHEFT \(877-438-4338\). If you have been the victim of identity theft, see) Tj T*
(www.IdentityTheft.gov and Pub. 5027.) Tj T*
(Go to www.irs.gov/IdentityTheft to learn more about identity theft and how to reduce your risk.) Tj T*
(Privacy Act Notice) Tj T*
(Section 6109 of the Internal Revenue Code requires you to provide your correct TIN to persons \(including) Tj T*
(federal agencies\) who are required to file information returns with the IRS to report interest, dividends,) Tj T*
(or certain other income paid to you; mortgage interest you paid; the acquisition or abandonment of) Tj T*
(secured property; the cancellation of debt; or contributions you made to an IRA, Archer MSA, or HSA. The) Tj T*
(person collecting this form uses the information on the form to file information returns with the IRS,) Tj T*
(reporting the above information. Routine uses of this information include giving it to the Department of) Tj T*
(Justice for civil and criminal litigation and to cities, states, the District of Columbia, and U.S.) Tj T*
(commonwealths and possessions for use in administering their laws.) Tj T*
(Form W-9 \(Rev. 3-2024\)) Tj T*
ET

endstream
